          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#TopologicalProperties Topological properties
          %p
          #CWComplexesAreLocallyContractible.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every CW-complex is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+topological+space"} locally contractible topological space
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")." do
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"} Hatcher 2002, prop. A.4
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes+are+paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"}> CW-complexes are paracompact Hausdorff spaces
                )
              %br/
              Every CW-complex is a
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
            %p
          %p
          #CWComplexIsCompactlyGenerated.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every CW-complex is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated topological space
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Since a CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              over attachments of standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-disks"} n-disks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{n_i}
              (its cells), by the characterization of colimits in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              (
              %a{:href => "Top#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"}> prop.
              ) a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is open or closed precisely if its restriction to each cell is open or closed, respectively. Since the
              = succeed "-disks" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              intersected with all compact subsets is closed, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is closed.
            %p
              For the converse direction, since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+CW-complex+is+a+Hausdorff+space"} a CW-complex is a Hausdorff space
              and since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
          %p In fact:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every CW-complex is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+topological+space"} Delta-generated topological space
          See there,
          %a{:href => "Delta-generated+topological+space#CWComplexesAreDTopologicalSpaces"} this Prop.
          %h3#products_of_cwcomplexes Products of CW-complexes
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
            is an inclusion of CW-complexes, then the quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/A
            is naturally itself a CW-complex, such that the quotient map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X/A
            is cellular.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a CW-complex and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complex"} finite CW-complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times K
            is naturally itself a CW-complex (see
            %a{:href => "#BrookeTaylor17"} Brooke-Taylor 2017
            for more and more generality, and see Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOfCWComplexesUnderCartesianProduct"}
            below).
          %p
            For example the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            of a CW-complex itself carries the structure of a CW-complex.
          %p
            Similarly for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
            CW-complexes: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of a pointed CW-complex with a finite pointed CW-complex is a pointed CW-complex. For example the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \wedge X
            of a pointed CW-complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is itself a CW-complex.
          #ClosureOfCWComplexesUnderCartesianProduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (product preserves CW-complexes in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
              with attaching maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\phi_\alpha\}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Psi_\beta\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-ification"} k-ification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \times Y)_c
              of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              (hence their Cartesian product in the category of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi Φ
                        %mi α
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Phi_\alpha \times \Psi_\beta\}
            %p
              If either of the two CW-complexes is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
              or if both are countable CW-complexes (have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
              of cells) then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X\times Y)_c \simeq X \times Y
            %p
              and so then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              itself has CW-complex structure.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"} Hatcher 2002, theorem A.6
          %h3#up_to_homotopy_equivalence Up to homotopy equivalence
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Every CW complex is homotopy equivalent to (the
              %a{:href => "simplicial+complex#geometric_realisations_and_polyhedra"} realization
              of) a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
          %p
            See
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Gray"} Gray
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+approximation"} CW approximation
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              Every CW complex is homotopy equivalent to a space that admits a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of a CW complex and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW+complex"} finite CW complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
              has the homotopy type of a CW complex.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Milnor59"}> Milnor 59
            )
          %h3#Subcomplexes Subcomplexes
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a CW complex, the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X' \hookrightarrow X
              of any subcomplex has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'
              %em
                %a{:href => "relative+homology#GoodPair"} good pair
              in the sense of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+homology"} relative homology
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"}> Hatcher 2002, prop. A.5
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              the inclusion of a subcomplex into a CW complex, then the pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
              is often called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-pair"} CW-pair
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#AGP02"}> AGP 02, def. 5.1.11
            )
          %h3#CellularApproximationTheorem Cellular approximation theorem
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+approximation+theorem"} cellular approximation theorem
            states that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
            (with chosen CW presentations) is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+map"} cellular map
            (a map induced by a morphism of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complexes"} cell complexes
          %p
            This is the analogue for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+approximation+theorem"} simplicial approximation theorem
            (sometimes also called lemma): that every continuous map between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realizations"} geometric realizations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            to a map induced by a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            (after subdivision).
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+approximation+theorem"} cellular approximation theorem
          %h3#fibrations Fibrations
          %p
            Fibrations between CW-complexes also behave particularly well:
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+Serre+fibration+between+CW-complexes+is+a+Hurewicz+fibration"} a Serre fibration between CW-complexes is a Hurewicz fibration
          %h3#SingularHomology Singular homology
          %p
            We discuss aspects of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(-) \colon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            of CW-complexes. See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+homology"} cellular homology
                of CW-complexes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a CW-complex and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_0 \hookrightarrow X_1 \hookrightarrow X_2 \hookrightarrow \cdots \hookrightarrow X
          %p
            for its
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtered topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n+1}
            the topological space obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
            by gluing on
            = succeed "-cells." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi nCells
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} nCells \in Set
            for the set of
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #SkeletalRelativeSingularHomologyOfCW.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
              of the filtering degrees is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi nCells
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi k
                              %mo =
                              %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X_k , X_{k-1})
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}[nCells] &amp; if\; k = n
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi nCells
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[nCells]
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on the set of
              = succeed "-cells." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The proof is spelled out at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "relative+homology#RelativeHomologyOfCWComplexes"} Relative singular homology - Of CW complexes
          #RelativeHomologyOfFilterStep.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k,n \in \mathbb{N}
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (k \gt n) \Rightarrow (H_k(X_n) \simeq 0)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a CW-complex of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+CW-complex"} dimension of a CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim X
              (the maximum degree of cells), then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi dim
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (k \gt dim X) \Rightarrow (H_k(X) \simeq 0).
            %p
              Moreover, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n
              the inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_k(X_n) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_k(X)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
              we have an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi image
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    image(H_n(X_n) \to H_n(X)) \simeq H_n(X)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is mostly for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"}> Hatcher 2002, lemma 2.34 b),c)
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+homology"} relative homology
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "relative+homology#LongExactSequences"} Relative homology – long exact sequences
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_{k+1}(X_n , X_{n-1})
                    \\to
                    H_k(X_{n-1})
                    \\to
                    H_k(X_n)
                    \\to
                    H_k(X_n, X_{n-1})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SkeletalRelativeSingularHomologyOfCW"}
              the leftmost and rightmost homology groups here vanish when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \neq n
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \neq n-1
              and hence exactness implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_k(X_{n-1})
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    H_k(X_n)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \neq n,n-1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p Finally for the last claim use that the above exact sequence gives
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_{n-1+1}(X_n , X_{n-1})
                    \\to
                    H_{n-1}(X_{n-1})
                    \\to
                    H_{n-1}(X_n)
                    \\to
                    0
            %p
              and hence that with the above the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{n-1}(X_{n-1}) \to H_{n-1}(X)
              is surjective.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Any undirected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              (loops and/or multiple edges allowed) has a geometric realization as a 1-dimensional CW complex.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              is a CW-complex (
              %a{:href => "#Milnor57"}> Milnor 57
              ).
            %p
              In particular, in the context of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+topological+spaces"} nice topological spaces
              maps each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              to a CW-complex.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
              have a standard CW-complex structure, with exactly 2-cells in each dimension, obtained
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} inductively
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+attachment"} attaching
              two
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hemispheres"} hemispheres
              to the
              = succeed "-sphere" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equator"} equator
              in the
              = succeed "-sphere." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+sphere"} infinite-dimensional sphere
            may be realized as the CW-complex which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over the resulting
            = succeed "-inclusions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \hookrightarrow S^{n + 1} \hookrightarrow S^{n + 2} \hookrightarrow \cdots
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
              over the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              has the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              with a single cell i in each dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2k
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4k
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+structure+of+K-projective+space"} cell structure of K-projective space
          %p
          #SmoothManifoldsAdmitCWComplexStructure.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (smooth manifolds)
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              admits a smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation"} triangulation
              (by the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation+theorem"} triangulation theorem
            %p
              In the generality of manifolds with group actions see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "G-CW+complex#GManifolds"} G-CW complex – G-manifolds
            %p
              Every noncompact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              to an
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#NapierRamachandran"} Napier &amp; Ramachandran
